IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `il37-nouns`
IMPORT `il37-xrefs`

-- Tests for the cross-references of ss 4A, 4B and 4(e), (f). Row IL-37.
-- A reference agrees when what the citing text says it points at is what the target says it is.
-- Positive control: a pair made to disagree must come out as disagreeing, so that "every reference agrees" is a reading and not a constant.

§ `Each cross-reference agrees`

#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4A(a)(1) to 4(e)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4A(b)(1) to 4(d)(2)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4A(b)(2) to 4(d)(3)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4A(c) to 4(a)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4A(d)(2) to 4(a)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B to 4(b)(1)(b)-(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4(e) to 4(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4(f)(2) to 4(b)(1)(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4(f)(3) to 4(d)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4(f)(3) to 4(e)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4(f)(3) to 4(d)(3)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(1) to Basic Law The Knesset s 9` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Knesset s 34` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Knesset s 36A` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Government s 11(b)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(2) to Basic Law The Government s 29(f)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 18` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 19` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 20` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 21` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(3) to Basic Law The Government s 29(a)` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `xref 4B(4) to Basic Law The Government s 28` EQUALS TRUE

§ `The whole list, and the control`

#ASSERT count `the cross-references of sections 4A, 4B and 4(e), (f)` EQUALS 22
#ASSERT `every cross-reference in the list agrees` `the cross-references of sections 4A, 4B and 4(e), (f)` EQUALS TRUE

-- A pair made to disagree (the citing text says elections, the target is a dissolution by law): the check must say so.
`a pair made to disagree` MEANS
    `A cross-reference` OF "control", "control", `the date of regular elections to the Knesset`, `dissolution of the Knesset by law`

#ASSERT `the cross-reference agrees` `a pair made to disagree` EQUALS FALSE
#ASSERT `every cross-reference in the list agrees` (LIST `a pair made to disagree`) EQUALS FALSE
